{
  "body_human_readable": "### Tesla's 2024 Deliveries Mark First Annual Decline in Over a Decade\n\nIn 2024, Tesla delivered a total of 1,789,226 vehicles globally, marking the first time in over a decade that the company has seen an annual decrease in deliveries. This represents a 1.1% dip from the 1,808,581 vehicles delivered in 2023.\n\nThe fourth quarter of 2024 saw a record for the company, with over 495,000 vehicles delivered. Despite this strong finish to the year, it was not enough to overcome a slower start to 2024.\n\nBreaking down the numbers for the year, the vast majority of deliveries were of the Model 3 and Model Y, which together accounted for 1,704,093 vehicles. The remaining 85,133 deliveries consisted of other models, including the Model S, Model X, and the newly introduced Cybertruck.\n\nIn terms of production, Tesla manufactured 1,773,443 vehicles in 2024, a figure slightly lower than its total deliveries for the year. This included 1,679,338 Model 3 and Model Y vehicles and 94,105 of its other models. The company's automotive revenue for the year saw a decrease of 6% to $77 billion.\n\nBeyond its automotive division, Tesla's energy business experienced significant growth, with energy storage deployments reaching a record 11.0 GWh in the fourth quarter.",
